From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:31:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pass vertical-align shifts to inline boxes

An atomic inline only knew baseline and middle, so vertical-align
lengths, percentages, sub and super all aligned at the baseline.
desmos.com's MathQuill exponent is an inline-block raised by .5em, so
x^2 rendered as x2.

Map baseline-shift to parley's Shift. A percentage is of the element's
own line-height. sub and super use Blink's offsets from the parent font
size. Line-relative top/center/bottom still align at the baseline.

Parley leaves a shifted box out of the line's ascent and descent, so the
strut pass for box-only lines adds the box's shifted extents back.
Without them it placed the line from the unshifted boxes alone and moved
a raised box above its line. The shift is fixed when the box is built,
so a vertical-align change now reconstructs the box.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: upstream maps vertical-align lengths,
percentages, sub, super, top and bottom onto parley's
InlineBox::vertical_align (stylo_to_parley::vertical_align), and parley
0.12 places shifted boxes in the line itself, so the construct and strut
halves are absorbed. Only the damage half remains: the alignment is
baked into the parley tree at construction, so a vertical-align change
still has to rebuild the box.
---
 src/layout/damage.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/layout/damage.rs b/src/layout/damage.rs
index 26cad40..7f7e0cf 100644
--- a/src/layout/damage.rs
+++ b/src/layout/damage.rs
@@ -451,6 +451,11 @@ pub(crate) fn compute_layout_damage(old: &ComputedValues, new: &ComputedValues)
             || old_box.position != new_box.position
             || old_box.contain != new_box.contain
             || old.clone_visibility() != new.clone_visibility()
+            // An atomic inline's vertical-align becomes its parley
+            // InlineBox::vertical_align when the box is constructed, so a change
+            // has to reconstruct it or the box keeps its old shift.
+            || old.clone_baseline_shift() != new.clone_baseline_shift()
+            || old.clone_alignment_baseline() != new.clone_alignment_baseline()
         {
             return true;
         }
